# .dockerignore = .gitignore for `docker build`.
# Everything listed here is INVISIBLE to COPY. Two reasons to care:
#
#   1. SPEED / CACHE: `COPY . .` hashes the whole build context. A stray
#      200 MB venv/ makes every build slow, and any file change (even a
#      .pyc) busts the COPY layer's cache for no reason.
#
#   2. SECRETS -- the horror story: someone runs `COPY . .` with a .env
#      full of production keys sitting in the folder. The keys are now
#      baked into an image layer FOREVER (deleting the file in a later
#      layer does NOT remove it from image history), and that image gets
#      pushed to a registry. Ignore .env here, always.

venv/            # the host's virtualenv -- the image pip-installs its own
__pycache__/     # host bytecode; wrong Python version anyway
*.pyc
.env             # secrets NEVER go into an image (see horror story above)
db.sqlite3       # local dev database is not code
.git             # whole repo history: big, and can contain old secrets
